        "alt": "First Paediatric Critical Care Simulation Series"
      }
    ],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Department of Paediatric and Child Health, in partnership with CIME, has successfully organised the first-ever Paediatric Critical Care Simulation Series (PCCSS). The aim is to equip healthcare providers in paediatric critical care with essential skills and knowledge to effectively manage critically ill children."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We're thrilled to share that 17 dedicated junior doctors actively participated in this groundbreaking session. Their commitment to advancing their expertise in paediatric critical care is truly commendable. The participants gained invaluable hands-on simulation experience, which was highly appreciated by both the faculty and attendees."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Together, we're making strides in enhancing the quality of care for critically ill children."
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            },
            {
              "type": "hard_break"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
